{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HNV2fQNk7ZkdsmurtwWJtV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `user` service is complete and verified. Everything passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `user` service from scratch against `SPEC.yaml` (a leaf service — empty `dependent_interface`).\n\n**Files created:**\n- `proto/v1/user.proto` — proto3, package `user.v1`, `go_package` → `api/v1;userv1`, service `UserService` with exactly the 5 spec RPCs (`CreateUser`, `GetUser`, `UpdatePreferences`, `GetPoints`, `AccrueOnBooking`) and matching request/response shapes.\n- `api/v1/user.pb.go` + `user_grpc.pb.go` — generated stubs.\n- `internal/server/server.go` — `NewServer()` returning `*Server`; all handlers with error codes per `error_semantics`:\n  - `InvalidArgument` for empty `user_id` (CreateUser/UpdatePreferences/AccrueOnBooking) and non-positive `amount`\n  - `AlreadyExists` on duplicate CreateUser\n  - `NotFound` for unknown users\n  - `AccrueOnBooking` does the read-modify-write under a `sync.Mutex` (`amount/100` integer division), serializing concurrent accruals.\n- `cmd/user/main.go` — gRPC on `:50051`, HTTP `/healthz`→200 on `:8080`, stdlib `log`, SIGTERM graceful shutdown, `//go:generate protoc …` directive.\n- `Makefile` (`build`/`test`/`image` with local-context docker build), `Dockerfile` (multi-stage → distroless static, exposes 50051/8080), and a tidied `go.mod` (third-party requires only).\n\n**Verification:**\n- `go build ./...` — OK\n- `go test ./...` — all pass, including `-race` (the concurrent-no-lost-updates test lands exactly at 500 points)\n- `go vet ./...` — clean\n\nOne environment note: the repo-root `go.work` lists 11 sibling services plus `tests/integration` that aren't present in this isolated checkout, so plain `go` commands fail on the missing modules. I generated stubs by invoking `protoc` directly and built/tested with `GOWORK=off`. When the full workspace is present (as in